# Services as Thin Orchestrators
RULE: Services are pure orchestrators using ServiceCLI. Delegate ALL business logic to unified libraries. No algorithms, parsers, or complex logic in services.
WHY: Business logic in libraries enables reuse across services. Services become thin adapters that compose library functions.
CODEX: 05-infrastructure/service-setup-checklist.md
DO: Delegate to UMI for market data; delegate to UTEI for execution; delegate to UDC for domain data; delegate to UTS for storage/secrets
NEVER: Implement business logic in services; duplicate code from libraries; parse API responses in services (use unified-api-contracts); complex algorithms in handlers
